{
 "duration": 76.369,
 "beats": [
  {
   "voice": "michael",
   "text": "What if you could never die? Not a longer life. No end at all.",
   "start": 0.0,
   "end": 4.312
  },
  {
   "voice": "michael",
   "text": "At first, it feels like a gift. Every language. Every place. No deadlines. No fear of running out of time.",
   "start": 4.662,
   "end": 12.593
  },
  {
   "voice": "michael",
   "text": "Today, the average person lives about seventy-three years. The longest verified life ever? One hundred twenty-two.",
   "start": 12.943,
   "end": 20.811
  },
  {
   "voice": "michael",
   "text": "You would blow past that record, and keep going. A thousand years is eight times the longest life on record.",
   "start": 21.161,
   "end": 28.094
  },
  {
   "voice": "michael",
   "text": "But everyone you love would grow old, and leave. Again, and again, and again. Even their faces would fade.",
   "start": 28.794,
   "end": 36.426
  },
  {
   "voice": "michael",
   "text": "Cities would rise and fall. Whole languages would vanish. Every country you knew would become a footnote.",
   "start": 36.776,
   "end": 43.071
  },
  {
   "voice": "michael",
   "text": "In about half a billion years, Earth may no longer support most plants. In about a billion, its oceans could boil away.",
   "start": 43.421,
   "end": 50.75
  },
  {
   "voice": "michael",
   "text": "Then, roughly five billion years from now, the Sun swells into a red giant. Earth is not expected to survive.",
   "start": 51.1,
   "end": 58.434
  },
  {
   "voice": "michael",
   "text": "But you would. Drifting through space, alive, in the dark, with nothing left to see.",
   "start": 59.134,
   "end": 64.755
  },
  {
   "voice": "michael",
   "text": "Nothing could end you. Nothing could change you. Maybe what gives life meaning, is that it ends. Every moment counts, because it's limited.",
   "start": 65.455,
   "end": 74.061
  },
  {
   "voice": "michael",
   "text": "So, would you take it?",
   "start": 74.761,
   "end": 76.369
  }
 ],
